md-bdc639b495c14646","cmd-826ca7d4a7344646","cmd-34bddb1256a24029","global:before_prepare:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct final-state and behavioral evidence. The mandatory restart protocol also demonstrates a pre-restart task baseline, acknowledged reboot scheduling, bounded loss of connectivity, a changed boot ID corroborated by the lifecycle snapshots, and recovery of login service, account data, home protections, and sudo authorization.","limitations":["The node was globally degraded before and after execution because of a pre-existing failed SSH service, so the restart evidence does not establish a wholly healthy systemd state; it does establish recovery of the task-relevant login service and account state (`cmd-c211048230c44b7a`, `cmd-4f006cd48695439a`, `cmd-826ca7d4a7344646`, `global:before_prepare:node1:failed-services`, `global:after_executor:node1:failed-services`).","No distinct cluster-state probe was captured during the restart protocol. The topology contains only this standalone managed node, and node reachability plus boot identity were recovered, but cluster health was not independently labeled or tested (`cmd-6183e47a784247e8`, `global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity`).","Password-related portions of some captured command text were distorted by redaction. Independent final checks still show an enabled password state and the required account, home, and sudo configuration (`cmd-966ead4176b64f73`, `cmd-826ca7d4a7344646`)."]}
